	"connections": [
		{
			"to": "western-civ/dna",
			"why": "Photo 51 and the King's measurements of a 34 Å turn with ten bases to it are the experimental side of the double helix that Watson and Crick's model of April 1953 explained."
		},
		{
			"to": "chemistry/crystallography",
			"why": "Photo 51 is X-ray diffraction applied to a fiber: the method the Braggs turned into a way of reading spacings, here reading a 3.4 Å stack and a 34 Å turn from the spacing of spots."
		},
		{
			"to": "chemistry/protein-structure",
			"why": "Pauling's triple-helix structure for DNA, early in 1953, was the manuscript Watson carried to King's on the day Wilkins showed him Photo 51."
